+Conclusion (bounded to this experiment). Infrastructure health alone does not establish appropriate model
+behavior. In these controlled scenarios, feature drift by itself could be operationally harmless, while large
+changes in model outputs and alert volume identified consequential behavior changes. The monitor therefore
+separates serving health, input/output drift, operational alert impact and retrospective model-performance
+evidence rather than treating all statistical drift as equivalent. Across 1,485 tested monitoring-setting
+combinations, the S0-S3 ordering remained unchanged. This suggests that the observed scenario separation is
