+5.4 The hypothesis as tested in the final run
+
+Infrastructure health checks and per-feature drift tests alone do not tell an operator whether the AI is still
+behaving appropriately or whether a change matters. A monitor that (1) reports serving status, (2) grades drift
+by its effect on the model's output and alert volume, and (3) reports retrospective model performance
+separately will separate no change, harmless change and consequential change in the controlled scenarios.
+
+What would count against it
+
+ • The monitor raises a drift severity (LOW or higher) on the no-change control S0.
+
+ • Its ordering does not match the intended operational interpretation, for example S1 HIGH or S3 OK.
