+6.4 Tier 3: retrospective model-performance diagnostic
+
+Once labels exist, Tier 3 reports PR-AUC, the prevalence baseline, lift (PR-AUC minus prevalence) and a 95%
+exploratory row-bootstrap interval for lift (1000 resamples, seed 0). The evaluation rows are sequentially
+dependent while the bootstrap resamples individual rows independently, so these intervals are used
+descriptively rather than as formally calibrated confidence intervals or hypothesis tests. Tier 3 is a separate
+retrospective diagnostic with an advisory follow-up action; it never sets drift severity or PAGE status. Display
+label when the interval's lower end is 0 or below: ABOVE-BASELINE PERFORMANCE NOT ESTABLISHED
+ON AVAILABLE DATA. On the available short, effectively in-sample dataset, PR-AUC does not establish
+performance above the prevalence baseline. This does not prove the model is useless or incapable of
+performing better on unseen data.
